==Middle English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|enm}} {{term|flet||lang=ang}}, {{term|flett||floor, ground; dwelling, house|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|enm}} {{recons|flatją||floor|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|enm}} {{recons|flataz||flat|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|enm}} {{recons|plat-||flat|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/flet/|lang=enm}}

===Noun===
{{enm-noun|pl=flets}}

# the [[floor]], [[ground]]
#: ''Cliued mi saule to þi '''flet'''.'' &mdash; Northern Verse Psalter, 1400
# a [[dwelling]], [[habitation]], [[house]], [[cottage]], [[hall]]
#: ''Þe lorde..Fyndez fire vpon '''flet''', þe [[freke]] þer byside.'' &mdash; Sir Gawain and the Green Knight, 1400
# A (level) piece of ground; a [[battlefield]]
#: ''Wiþ four othre meteþ he ... & fuld hem on þe '''flette'''.'' &mdash; Sir Firumbras, c1380

====Descendants====
* English [[flat]]

====References====
* Middle English Dictionary, flet

