==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|fled}}, {{l|ang|flett}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|flatją||floor|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|flataz||flat|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|plat-||flat|lang=ine-pro}}. Akin to {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|flet|flet, flette|lang=ofs|dwelling, house}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/flet/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|g=n|pl=flet}}

# the [[floor]], [[ground]]
#: ''Heó on '''flet''' gecrong'' &mdash; She sank to the ground.
# a [[dwelling]], [[habitation]], [[house]], [[cottage]], [[hall]]
#: ''Gif ðæt '''flet''' geblódgad wyrþe.'' &mdash; If the house be stained with blood.

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-n|flet}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[fletræst]] f. — couch
* [[fletsittend]] m. — sitter in hall, courtier, guest.
* [[fletwerod]] n. — hall-troop, body-guard

=====Descendants=====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|flet}}
** English [[flat]]

===Etymology 2===
Likely from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|flutōną||to float|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|plewd-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|plew-||to float, swim, fly|lang=ine-pro}}; compare {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|fløde||cream|lang=da}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|fleytið||skimming|lang=is}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|fløte||cream|lang=no}}

====Pronunciation====
{{rfp|lang=ang|if the same as ety 1, then remove this Pron section and move Ety 1 Pron above ety 1 as level 3 hdr))}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|ang|flete}}, {{l|ang|fliet}}, {{l|ang|flyte}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|g=f|head=flēt|pl=flēta}}

# [[cream]], [[skimming]], [[curds]]
#: ''Hwít sealt dó on reám oððe góde '''fléte'''. &mdash; Put white salt into cream or good skimmings.

